      "title": "Digital Calendar Assembly",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": false,
      "reverse": true,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "d, m, y = input().split()\nday1 = input()\ndays_in_month = int(input())\n\n#find start day position\nstart = ['Monday','Tuesday','Wednesday','Thursday','Friday','Saturday','Sunday'].index(day1)\n\n#fill calendar\ncal_days = [['  ' for i in range(7)] for j in range(6)]\nfor i in range(days_in_month):\n    row, col = divmod(start+i,7)\n    day_num = f\"{i+1:02}\"\n    if day_num == d: cal_days[row][col] = 'XX' #mark current day\n    else: cal_days[row][col] = day_num\n\n#print top border\nprint('-'*22)\n#print year\nprint(f\"|{' '*15}{y} |\")\n#print month\nprint(f\"| {m}{' '*(19-len(m))}|\")\n#print empty line (with borders)\nprint(f\"|{' '*20}|\")\n#print days of week\nprint(\"|MO TU WE TH FR SA SU|\")\n#print separator line (dashes)\nprint(f\"|{'-'*20}|\")\n#print weeks of month\nfor i in cal_days: print(f\"|{' '.join(i)}|\")\n#print bottom border\nprint('-'*22)",
      "statement": "Given a [[date]], the [[day]] that was or will be the {{1st}} of that [[Month]] and the [[days in Month]], build and print the calendar page for that [[Month]].\n\n<<Explanation of the calendar format>>\n```\n---------------------- Fixed\n|               2026 | Right-align [[YYYY]] + a space\n| May                | Left-align a space + [[Month]]\n|                    | Fixed\n|MO TU WE TH FR SA SU| Fixed\n|--------------------| Fixed\n|            XX 02 03| Week 1\n|04 05 06 07 08 09 10| Week 2\n|11 12 13 14 15 16 17| Week 3\n|18 19 20 21 22 23 24| Week 4\n|25 26 27 28 29 30 31| Week 5\n|                    | Week 6\n---------------------- Fixed\n```\nEach week row contains {{7}} space-separated values. Each value is either a day number (with a leading {{0}} if necessary) or {{2}} spaces, except for the current date, for which the value will be {{XX}}.",
